                <pb facs="1026" n="902" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg902"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/178: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Mission at Lausanne to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lausanne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-22T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 22,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>11. The powers will not be inclined to ask for measures of relief for the
                    Armenians which would involve territorial sacrifices by Turkey, as Angora
                    objects intensely to any reduction of its territory to form areas of refuge for
                    minorities. To what extent should we go in raising and supporting a point which
                    may not be accepted and which will arouse Turkey’s resentment?</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
